  "steps": [
    "Boil the soya chunks, squeeze out all the excess water and keep them aside.",
    "Thinly slice 2 medium onions and air-fry at 180°C with a light spray of oil until brown and crisp.",
    "Make the marinade by mixing the soya chunks, mushrooms, Skyr, ¾ of the air-fried onions, chopped coriander and mint, biryani masala, kasuri methi, red chilli powder, salt, green chilli-garlic paste, lemon juice and jaggery powder. Mix well and let it rest for 10–15 minutes.",
    "Cook the Daawat Brown Basmati Rice with cinnamon, black peppercorns, 1 tsp ghee and a pinch of salt until 90% cooked. Drain and keep aside.",
    "Heat 1 tsp ghee in a pan and add cumin seeds. Let them sizzle, then add the entire marinated soya-mushroom mixture. Cook on low heat for 10–12 minutes.",
    "Layer the 90% cooked rice over the soya-mushroom mixture. Top with the remaining ¼ air-fried onions, fresh mint and saffron-infused milk.",
    "Cover and cook on low heat for another 6–7 minutes, allowing the rice to finish cooking and the flavours to infuse."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The creator uses Daawat brown basmati rice for its higher fibre, which slows the blood sugar rise, and made this for World Heart Day.",
